course: dictionary
lesson: 1887
title: Learning a word from its sense
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is in use. The word collie is a good example. «A collie has a long pointed nose and thick fur» tells you it is a breed of dog. «A Border collie herds sheep by running around them» tells you that a Border collie is a working dog on a farm.
explain: Look at the words near the hard word to find its sense. In «A Border collie called Chaser learned the names of over 1,000 toys», the words Chaser and toys show you that this collie is a dog that learns. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence best?
explain: Some words come from a place or a job. The collie was first used in Scotland to herd sheep, so the word has links to farm life. When you meet a new word, ask what the people who use it do, and where they live.
fact: A collie is a breed of dog with a long pointed nose and thick fur.
fact: A Border collie is a very clever working sheepdog, often black and white.
fact: Collies were first used in Scotland to herd sheep.
fact: «Herd» means to gather animals together and move them as a group.
fact: A word can have more than one meaning, so always check the sentence to see which one is meant.
exercise: «A collie has a long pointed nose and thick fur.» What is a collie? | *A breed of dog | A kind of sheep | A type of bird | A farm building
exercise: «A Border collie herds sheep by running around them.» What does herds mean here? | Shears the wool off | *Gathers and moves together | Sleeps near | Feeds on grass
exercise: In «A Border collie called Chaser learned the names of over 1,000 toys», which word tells you Chaser is a dog? | toys | learned | *collie | names
test: What does «Border collie» mean? | *A very clever working sheepdog, often black and white | A long pointed nose on a sheep | A toy with thick fur | A kind of cat that lives on farms
test: «Chaser learned the names of over 1,000 toys.» What kind of dog is Chaser? | A bulldog | *A border collie | A greyhound | A poodle
exam: «The shepherd used whistles to guide the collie across the hillside.» What does guide mean? | Clean | Sleep | *Lead or direct | Feed
